test tests::read_command_unknown_flag_exits_two ... ok
clio setup [--type zero-dependency|airgapped|custom] [--yes] [--config PATH]
          [--embed online|local] [--embed-url U] [--embed-model M] [--embed-key K]
          [--embed-provider tei|openai] [--embed-dims N]
          [--rerank online|local] [--rerank-url U] [--rerank-model M] [--rerank-key K]
          [--rerank-provider tei|cohere]
          [--extract local|skip|online] [--compose-dir DIR]

Configure the stack for one install type and write the deployment config the
binary reads without any environment variable.

Install types:
  zero-dependency  hosted embed + rerank; no Docker
  airgapped        the local Docker stack; endpoints point at 127.0.0.1
  custom           choose online or local per service

Every prompt has a flag equivalent: non-interactive runs (piped stdin, --yes, or
--non-interactive) never prompt and fail fast when a required flag is missing.
The default config path is $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/clio/deployment.json
(fallback ~/.config/clio/deployment.json); --config overrides it and
CLIO_DEPLOYMENT_CONFIG overrides the default (an empty value disables loading).
Hosted extraction is not available yet; --extract online is reported and skipped.
